=begin

  osa-sail.lic: sail your own OSA ship from port to port.

    ;osa-sail <port>            retrieve or board your ship, sail to <port>, step onto the pier
    ;osa-sail route <port>      show the course only, send nothing
    ;osa-sail ports             list the ports
    ;osa-sail help

  Options (one trip):
    --call-wind       cast Breeze (612) or Call Wind (912) into each sail; Breeze is recast from its
                      level-based duration ((3 * level / 9) * 9 s), Call Wind every 90 s
    --no-confirm      skip the plan confirmation
    --no-watch        do not send WATCH OCEAN
    --flag-wait       if the white flag is on cooldown, wait up to 10 min for it (default: sail at once and outrun trouble)
    --hull=<name>     name the hull when SHIP INFO cannot be read (sloop, brigantine, carrack, galleon, frigate, man o' war)

  The ship is left at the far pier. Nothing is stored.

  The ocean grid, the ports, the piers and the course search were designed and mapped by Nisugi.
  Deck layouts for every hull come from the community OSA scripts (Peggyanne's osacrew ship table,
  Selfane's osamap) and are being verified hull by hull.

        author: Nisugi
  contributors: Nisugi
          game: gs
          tags: travel, osa, ship, sailing
      required: Lich >= 5.12.0
       version: 0.1.0

  Version Control:
    Major_change.feature_addition.bugfix
  0.1.0 (2026-11-09)
    - first version: port to port on your own ship, any hull, sloop verified

=end

module OsaSail
  VERSION = '0.1.0'

